68</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-61285763-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>61285763</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8148675-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>8148675</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1041643A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI ELECTRIC CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMINAGA SHUUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMINAGA, SHUUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMINAGA SHUUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMINAGA, SHUUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A Schottky diode, particularly, used in combination with an insulated gate semiconductor device, which has a structure with no PN junction and has an increased breakdown voltage against a reverse bias. The diode includes a P-type impurity region (12) which is exposed from the surface of an N-type semiconductor substrate (11) serving as a drain and whose surface functions as a channel region, and a gate insulation layer (32) covering the P-type impurity region (12). The gate electrode (53) extends from above the gate insulation layer (32) to a first taper of the oxide layer (31). Also disclosed is a Schottky diode (103) which has a semiconductor substrate (11) as a cathode and a boundary layer (14) as a Schottky region, where the anode electrode (54) extends from above the boundary layer (14) to a second taper of the oxide layer (31) which is formed above the end of the boundary layer (14).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne en particulier une diode Schottky, utilisée en association avec un dispositif à semiconducteur à grille isolée, dont la structure est dépourvue de jonction PN et présente une tension de rupture accrue s'opposant à une polarisation inverse. Cette diode comprend une zone d'impuretés de type p (12) exposée sur la surface d'un substrat à semiconducteur de type n (11), servant de drain et dont la surface fonctionne comme une zone canal, et une couche d'isolation de grille (32) recouvrant la zone d'impuretés de type p (12). L'électrode de grille (53) s'étend du dessus de la couche d'isolation de grille (32) jusqu'au premier cône de la couche d'oxyde (31). En outre, cette invention concerne une diode Schottky (103) comportant un substrat à semiconducteur (11) comme cathode, et une couche limite (14) comme zone de Schottky, l'électrode d'anode (54) s'étendant du dessus de la couche limite (14) jusqu'à un second cône de la couche d'oxyde (31) formée au-dessus de l'extrémité de la couche limite (14).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>